{
  "dom_id": "step-q325901",
  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Complete the following parametric equations generating the hyperbola $2{x}^{2}-8{y}^{2}=16$ in terms of the parameter $t,$ defined for $t\\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ]$ where $t\\ne \\pm \\frac{\\pi }{2}.$\n\n$x=2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sec}\u2061t,\\,$\n$y=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "The parametric equations of a horizontal hyperbola with Cartesian equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1\n$$\n\nare given by\n\n$$\nx=a\\operatorname{sec}\u2061t,\\,y=b\\operatorname{tan}\u2061t.\n$$\n\nFirst, we rewrite the equation of our hyperbola in standard form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2{x}^{2}-8{y}^{2} & =16 \\\\ \\frac{2{x}^{2}}{16}-\\frac{8{y}^{2}}{16} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have $a=\\sqrt{8}=2\\sqrt{2}$ and $b=\\sqrt{2}.$ Therefore, the parametric equations are\n\n$$\nx=2\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sec}\u2061t,\\,y=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{tan}\u2061t.\n$$",
